//  Why A is stored transposed (As[k][row]): the thread's 8 accumulator rows
//  then read 8 CONSECUTIVE shared addresses at a fixed k, so a float4 read
//  covers 4 rows; this keeps the read vectorizable. cp.async writes
//  contiguous bytes, so it cannot transpose during the copy; therefore A is
//  filled by a short synchronous global->shared transpose (global float4 over
//  k -> 4 scalar stores), while B keeps its natural col-major-in-shared
//  layout and IS loaded with cp.async for latency hiding.

